  "worked_solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $r$ and $q$ have the opposite directions. So, $r\\ne 3q.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $s$ and $t$ are parallel and have the same directions. Also, the magnitude of $s$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $t.$ So, $s=2t.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $p$ and $s$ are parallel and have the opposite directions. Also, their magnitudes are the same. So, $p=-s.$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, and statement I is false.",
